FILE: app/src/skip-to-end.ts
```ts
import { goToFrame } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import type { AnimationGroup } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function skipToEnd(group: AnimationGroup): void {
    const frameRate = group.frameRate ?? 60;
    const lastFrame = group.duration * frameRate;

    goToFrame(group, lastFrame);
    group.currentTime = group.duration;
}
```

I created `src/skip-to-end.ts` which seeks the group to its final frame via `goToFrame` (which writes the last keyframe values and pauses the group), then explicitly sets `currentTime` to `duration` so the progress bar reads 100%. I was slightly uncertain whether `goToFrame` at exactly the end time on a *looping* glTF group yields the end pose or wraps to the start; the notes say "past the end wraps," which I read as strictly past, so exactly-at-end should give the final pose.
